ticket_data.description:
If a `SeparateDatabaseAndState` has an operation on an unrelated model before an `AlterField` that retypes a primary key, the foreign keys to that primary key keep their old type. The same operations without `SeparateDatabaseAndState` retype them. I reproduced using postgres, on Django 5.2, 6.0, 6.1, and main.

Start with these models:

{{{#!python
class Parent(models.Model):
    id = models.AutoField(primary_key=True)

class Child(models.Model):
    parent = models.ForeignKey(Parent, models.CASCADE)

class Confounder(models.Model):
    pass
}}}

